Elex - is old school open world action RPG, that gives countless hours of exploring, combat, quests and interesting story line. Main thing, thet you need to keep in mind, its is not a AAA experience.

Pros:
- big intricate open world;
- interesting and memorable characters;
- many quest with variety of ways to complete them;
- 3 completely different factions;
- interesting storyline;
- deep lore;

Cons:
- very steep difficulty curve;
- janky animations;
- reskin enemy;

TLDR: This game does not worth your time if you are used to play AAA loot-based open world RPGs (Skyrim, Fallout, Witcher 3, you name it).

This game is disappointing and i will explain why.

To begin with, i love post-apocalypse, the world after the catastrophe, etc. So I was pretty patient and excited about the Elex at my first 14-15 hours. But when the (combat) events began to re-occur and so-called "gameplay loop" did not get better but worse (i started to die even more often with almost no new gear on the horizon)... Then my interest began to fade away pretty quickly (like really quick - in 1 hour my excitement went from 80-70 to 0%).

I think It is better to compare this game with Fallout 4 ("Skyrim with guns"), because it is similar to the the Elex and a lot of people played it.

Okay. Imagine Fallout 4:
- with very uneven plot, quests, map and sound designs;
- Fallout 4 where you constantly fighting Death Claws, Behemots and Feral Ghouls, like at every corner of the game... and suddenly when you get better weapon GRADE (like sword v2 form example) they all become weak cockroaches;
- with 2-3 melee weapons and 3-4 guns;
- Fallout 4 where you will play with melee weapons for like 10-20 hours (Gothic with guns, yeah right) and then you will get laser(!) gun that cannot kill monsters even with 4 ammo clips so you will grab your trusty sword and board again... if you dont wanna die in 2 melee hits or kite and fly (jetpack yeah!) around like a mad chicken;
- with shitty graphical effects (some of them reminded me of these games from the early 2000s, especially these shitty status effects and spitting enemies. Also there are no footprints in the snow and sand, and snow and sand are everywhere in the Elex) and very uneven graphics (from WOW this is beautiful to WTH is this low-poly and non-textured shit in like 50 meters);
- with awful melee (how can it even possible? smack-smack-hit-Q, zero feedback or sense of weapon) and terrible ranged combat. There is like zero level satisfaction from killing blows;
- with dead or rather static world (monsters/NPCs fighting with each other, that all you have - no other random events at all);
- and finally - with boring exploration (you CAN explore the world for the sake of exploration but you will get shitty or no rewards at all most of the time).

Do you want to play this version of Fallout 4 or you would rather buy cheap Gold Edition of Assassin's Creed Origins / Assassin's Creed Odyssey at the sale to satisfy your desire in open world games as i did some hours ago?

